## User identity & data scoping

Today everything lives in a single `data/` store. We need a stable **user id** across channels:

| Channel | Identity source |
|---------|-----------------|
| Web | Thirdweb wallet address and/or verified phone from in-app wallet |
| Telegram | `telegramUserId` + optional linked phone |
| WhatsApp | E.164 sender phone |

**Linking:** A user who starts on web and later uses Telegram should map to one `userId` (e.g. phone verification or “link Telegram” in profile). Store:

- `users/{userId}/contacts.json`
- `users/{userId}/history.json`
- `users/{userId}/preferences.json` (limits, default corridor, language)

Agent API requests include `x-user-id` or signed session JWT from web; Telegram/WhatsApp pass `senderPhone` / `telegramUserId` in `TransferContext` (already partially supported via `senderPhone`).

