## Implementation phases

### Phase 0 — Telegram-first onboarding
- [ ] `GET /api/user/status` + `POST /api/user/link` (`telegramUserId` ↔ wallet)
- [ ] Web `/auth?tg=` — Thirdweb signup + auto-link + redirect home
- [ ] Web `/deposit?tg=` — deposit flow with return-to-Telegram CTA
- [ ] Bot: welcome, inline buttons, state-aware replies (unknown → wallet → deposit → send)
- [ ] `remifi-api user status --telegram-id` for OpenClaw skill
- [ ] Balance refresh after deposit (poll or webhook → proactive Telegram message)

### Phase 1 — Per-user data + one-tap web sends
- [ ] `userId` model and scoped `contacts` / `history` on agent API
- [ ] Web: pass wallet address on `/api/intent` and `/api/transfer/prepare`
- [ ] `POST /api/transfer/prepare` + `POST /api/transfer/confirm` (split prepare/sign)
- [ ] `PayChat` confirm button → Thirdweb `sendTransaction` (in-app wallet, no MetaMask)
- [ ] Default connect flow: in-app wallet only; external wallets behind "Advanced"
- [ ] Funding checks against **user** balance (public address), not agent wallet
- [ ] Telegram: quote in chat → confirm link → web one-tap sign

### Phase 2 — User-funded escrow + claim hardening
- [ ] User-signed `RemifiVault.deposit` (replace agent `executeEscrowRemittance` for production)
- [ ] Deploy / configure `REMIFI_VAULT_ADDRESS` on target network
- [ ] Claim page: phone OTP vs `phoneHash` before claim
- [ ] After claim: upsert contact `walletAddress` for sender’s book

### Phase 3 — Channel parity & polish
- [ ] Web-first users: `/profile` → “Connect Telegram” (reverse link)
- [ ] “Chat on Telegram” CTA across web shell
- [ ] Telegram Web App mini-browser for auth/deposit without leaving Telegram
- [ ] Recipient notifications (Twilio) when sender opts in
- [ ] Spending limits per `userId` (not global agent limits)

